,\"ref\":\"d51\",\"snippet\":\" ... Over a career spanning more than twenty years, he has translated a wide variety of authors, including Michel Houellebecq, Patrick Modiano, Emiliano Monge, Alice Zeniter and Virginie Despentes. His translations have garnered a number of award, including the IMPAC Dublin Literary Award (2002) and the Independent Foreign Fiction ... \",\"title\":\"https://fivebooks.com/best-books/the-best-of-world-literature-the-2022-international-booker-prize-shortlist-frank-wynne/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... All the Lives We Never Lived won the Sahitya Akademi, one of India's highest literary honours, and was shortlisted for the International Dublin Literary Award. It won Tata Literature Live Book of the Year. The Folded Earth won the Economist Crossword Prize and her latest book, The ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d37\"},\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... and is shortlisted for the Dublin Literary Award and the Climate Fiction Prize, among others. Marosia Castaldi's The Hunger of Women wins the ALTA Prize for Prose (for the best translation from any language), Phantom Pain Wings wins the 2024 National Book Critics Circle Award for Poetry ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d38\"},\"ref\":\"d38\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022 Dublin Literary Award. That program's €100,000 purse (US$107,179)—as opposed to the 50-50 split of the International Booker prize—is split 75-25, with €75,000 going to the author.\\n\\nWynne became something of an international local hero—local to translation—earlier ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d52\"},\"ref\":\"d52\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was also awarded France's Prix Femina for a work in translation. Her seventh novel, Someone, was a New York Times bestseller, a finalist for the Dublin IMPAC Award, the National Book Critics Circle Award, the Patterson Prize for Fiction, and the Dayton Literary Peace Prize. Three ... \",\"title\":\"https://missionandministry.georgetown.edu/conference-participants/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1995-02-23\\n---\\nFiction\\n\\nAlthough I work in many genres, I am best known for my fiction, which has been translated into over forty languages.\\n\\nThe Paris Express (2025) is about a French railway disaster of 1895, and was inspired by an iconic, surreal photograph of the aftermath ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.emmadonoghue.com/emma-donoghue.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\" ... If the winning title is a translation, the author receives €75,000, while the translator is awarded €25,000. In 2025, the Dublin Literary Award will proudly commemorate its 30th anniversary.\\n\\n2025 SHORTLIST REVEALED\\n\\nDiscover this year's Shortlist\\n\\nFEATURES\\n\\nPREVIOUS WINNERS\\n\\n2024\\n\\n2023\\n\\n2022\\n\\n2021\",\"title\":\"https://dublinliteraryaward.ie/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... His work has been translated into more than thirty languages, and has been presented with numerous awards, including the Chevalier de l'Ordre des Artes et des Lettres, Prix Medicis, the Peace Prize of the German Booksellers Association and most recently the 2017 Man Booker International Prize. He ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ibby.org/subnavigation/archives/hans-christian-andersen-awards/2020\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d55\"},\"ref\":\"d55\",\"snippet\":\" ... only on the everyday life of a non-elite Middle Eastern translator, but on an array of international clients. We'll encounter Armenian and Persian translators working for the 18th century East India Company and literary translators negotiating with their editors in a time of heavy censorship in ... \",\"title\":\"https://blogs.bl.uk/english-and-drama/visual-arts/page/2/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"51ca3e6b68fe8d85650d83b42c9948cf60b070aea3b85cebdacf6d118ee90d8a\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"e81d058c357bc0160b46ed66df13d758c5e0c11c7c29f3384797ebd11d924981\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Dublin Literary Award shortlist translated over twenty languages\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_d0327929e3cb4a19afdc695d"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d38\"},\"ref\":\"d38\",\"snippet\":\" ... exuberant, coruscating translation.\\n\\n\\\"This is a luminous novel of India and Partition, but one whose spellbinding brio and fierce compassion weaves youth and age, male and female, family and nation into a kaleidoscopic whole.\\\"\\n\\nThe International Booker Prize 2022 Shortlist\\n\\n| Title | Author | Translator | Original Language | Author Residence | Publisher ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... Unlike the Booker Prize, short story collections are eligible for the International Booker Prize. The £50,000 prize money is split evenly between the author and translator of the winning novel.\\n\\nHistory and administration\\n\\nThe prize was established as the \\\"Booker Prize for Fiction\\\" after the company Booker ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... fifth novel, Swimming Home, no one took it. That it was ever even published – earning the first of her two Booker shortlistings, in 2012 – owed to the disillusionment of former Amazon employee Stefan Tobler, now 49, then working as a freelance translator assessing potential foreign-language acquisitions for ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2024 Booker International Prize Winner:\\n\\nKairos by Jenny Erpenbeck translated by Michael Hofmann\\n\\n2024 Booker International Prize Shortlist finalists:\\n\\n-\\n\\nNot a River by Selva Almada\\n\\n-\\n\\nMater 2-10 by Hwang Sok-yong\\n\\n-\\n\\nWhat I'd Rather Not Think About by Jente Posthuma\\n\\n-\\n\\nCrooked Plow by Itamar Vieira Junior ... \",\"title\":\"https://bookclubs.com/blog/2023-2024-book-awards-and-book-prize-winners\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d37\"},\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2019\\n\\nNo major changes for the press, but another good year for prize attention. Amy Arnold's Slip of a Fish landed a 2019 Goldsmiths Prize shortlisting, while Alia Trabucco Zerán's The Remainder was shortlisted for the Man Booker International Prize. Multiple translation prize wins and shortlistings ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... The International Booker Prize is awarded every year for a book that is translated into English and published in the UK or Ireland.\\n\\nShree's novel competed against five other shortlisted titles, by Mieko Kawakami, Bora Chung, Jon Fosse, Claudia Pineiro and former winner Olga Tokarczuk.\\n\\nBorn in ... \",\"title\":\"https://literaturecurry.com/news-details/1159/ge