edia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... Though the most recent Nobel prize in literature winner Han Kang was eligible for this year's prize with her book We Do Not Part, translated from Korean by e. yaewon and Paige Aniyah Morris, she did not make the list. Kang won the International Booker in 2016 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2025/feb/25/all-13-writers-on-international-booker-longlist-are-first-time-nominees\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... that more than her career is in danger, she hides her editor beneath her floorboards, and together, as fear and loss close in around them, they cling to literature as the last way of preserving the past. Finalist for the International Booker Prize and the National Book Award ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nypl.org/spotlight/world-literature-festival/recommended-translations\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d23\"},\"ref\":\"d23\",\"snippet\":\" ... to assert that his novel, The Sea, was more literary than 'the normal kind of Booker book'. When the interviewer suggested that all Booker Prize winners were literary fiction, he replied:\\n\\n'Yeeees, the Booker winner will be a literary book. But I feel that over the past 15 ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... His first two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were both finalists for the Booker prize. His novels have been translated into more than 29 languages and won the inaugural FT/Oppenheimer Award for Fiction, an NAACP Image Award, the LA Times Book prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"31c7904fcc5ba2049954e9226a21652770b2c64fe3bb09ccf36bb10b2e7366a1\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"248d6faf2b9e92d8cb34cec682984ab1f8ccbdab7ddba2fd399119f47fd73946\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"book translated more than 25 languages International Booker Prize contender\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_465f29309b4f43d2881c03f5"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure. The key insight: \"the award itself was originally created in the 2000s.\" The International Booker Prize was established in 2005. Let me think about the timeline:\n\n- Book A published in the 2010s, was a contender for the International Booker Prize, translated into 25+ languages\n- In the year Book A was published, Book B won the International Booker Prize\n- Book B was released the preceding year\n- Author of Book B born in city where Author of Book A grew up\n\nLet me look at the International Booker Prize winners in the 2010s and check the timeline. The 2017 winner was \"The Unseen\" by Roy Jacobsen. Let me search for books translated into 25+ languages that were contenders.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize 2017 winner The Unseen Roy Jacobsen\", \"International Booker Prize winners list 2010s by year\", \"Man Booker International Prize 2016 2017 2018 winner\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_cb1dd0f0d99a4ffa95447f3b","index":0,"